CORE
template-fields.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[shell-dynamic-site\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.1\] .* the parts of the text of eval for the holes of "set -- -v "\* have no character .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.1\] .* = -v: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-argument-count\.1\] .*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The hole's part is split into fields with the default IFS, as parsing the
text would: here, lower-case words and blanks. (cvc5 is slow on field
splitting of unknown values, with or without eval.)
